{{ill|Konpira Kaido|ja|金毘羅街道}} is a pilgrimage route of {{ill|Kotohira Shrines|lt=Kotohira Shrines|ja|金刀比羅神社}} located in {{ill|Japan|simple}}. It connects many Konpira Shrines.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Arched Stone Bridge {{!}} FACILITIES {{!}} GUIDE |url=http://www.shikokumura.or.jp/en/guide/facilities/arched-stone-bridge/ |access-date=2023-09-17 |website=SHIKOKUMURA |language=ja}}</ref> It is a [[Kaidō]].




{{ill|Kotohira Shrines|ja|金刀比羅神社}} are [[shinto shrine]]s dedicated to [[Ōmononushi]]. Due to [[Shinbutsu-shūgō]] they often also worship [[Konpira Gongen]]

They are part of the famous Inahachikonten Shrines (稲八金天神社)  of the [[Shrine Consolidation Policy]] alongside [[Inari Shrine]], [[Hachiman Shrine]], {{ill|Kotohira Shrines|ja|金刀比羅神社}}, and [[Tenmangū|Tenmangu Shrine]].

