== '''Marugame Kaidō''' (丸亀街道) (Konpira Orai, 金毘羅往来)
==
{| 
|-
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Kagawa|number=4|align=left}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Kagawa|number=204|align=left}} 
|}
Starting from {{ill|Marugame Port|ja|丸亀港|12=draft}}, this route proceeds via Nakabu, Gunke, Yokita, and others to Kotohira. Because the overland distance was short and the terrain flat, many pilgrims—arriving by {{ill|Konpira Ship|ja|金毘羅船|12=draft}} from places such as {{ill|Osaka|ja|大坂|12=draft}} or from {{ill|Bizen Province|ja|備前国|12=draft}}—used it. It is said that during the {{ill|Enkyō era|ja|延享|12=draft}} a regular ship service operated between Osaka and Marugame, making it the busiest of the many Konpira Kaidō routes. Today, roads following its course include {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 204 Marugame Station Line|ja|香川県道204号丸亀停車場線|lt=Kagawa Prefectural Route 204|lt_ja=香川県道204号|12=draft}} and {{ill|Kagawa/Tokushima Prefectural Route 4 Marugame-Miyoshi Line|ja|香川県道・徳島県道4号丸亀三好線|lt=Prefectural Route 4|lt_ja=香川県道4号}}.

At {{ill|Marugame Port|ja|丸亀港|12=draft}}, from the Taisuke lantern or from the {{ill|Sanuki Hamakaidō|ja|さぬき浜街道|12=draft}} ({{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 193 Kawazu-Marugame Line|ja|香川県道193号川津丸亀線|lt=Kagawa Prefectural Route 193|lt_ja=香川県道193号|12=draft}}) beneath the Kyogoku Ohashi—where {{ill|Kyogoku Funatama Shrine|ja|京極船魂神社|12=draft}} is located—head south along a municipal road toward {{ill|Marugame Station|ja|丸亀駅|12=draft}}. Pass under the elevated structure of the {{ill|Yosan Line|ja|予讃線|12=draft}}, and at Tsūchō turn west. In front of Marugame Station, after crossing {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 204 Marugame Station Line|ja|香川県道204号丸亀停車場線|lt=Kagawa Prefectural Route 204|lt_ja=香川県道204号|12=draft}}, immediately enter the museum street of Hamamachi (a narrow lane located about 50 m west of the intersection—with the south side of the {{ill|Inokuma Genichirō Contemporary Art Museum|ja|猪熊弦一郎現代美術館|12=draft}}) and proceed south through Nanjō Town to Nakabu Town. In Nakabu (at the marker of “Torinomeken”), turn west; however, the road descends to the southwest, passing through Nakabu’s large torii gate and continuing south. Then cross {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 205|ja|香川県道205号|12=draft}}, and at the three‐way intersection of Nakabu’s three houses (marked by the Heisei-era five‐stone marker) turn east; next, cross {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 33|ja|香川県道33号|12=draft}} and enter Yamakita Town. From the Castle West Community Center in Yamakita, turn south onto {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 204|ja|香川県道204号|12=draft}} and enter Katsubaru Town; after passing in front of the Marugame Castle South Post Office, at a fork marked by the Heisei-era twenty-stone marker, turn west—leaving Prefectural Route 204 onto a municipal road along the town boundary—and proceed south. Cross {{ill|National Route 11|ja|国道11号|12=draft}}, pass along the eastern edge of Tamura Pond (a local reservoir, {{ill|Reservoir|ja|溜め池|12=draft}}), and continue further south; then, passing under the Takamatsu Expressway overpass where a lantern is visible on the west side of the road, proceed south toward Gunke Town. In Sanjō Town, merge with {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 4|ja|香川県道4号|12=draft}} and enter Yokita Town in {{ill|Zentsūji City|ja|善通寺市|12=draft}}. Thereafter, continuing almost along Route 4, from Yokita Town pass through {{ill|Mannou Town|ja|まんのう町|12=draft}} (Kōmon and Mannou Town Nishitakashino) and at Naeda in {{ill|Kotohira Town|ja|琴平町|12=draft}}, turn west. After passing through the precinct alley of {{ill|Wakamiya Shrine|ja|若宮神社|12=draft}}, continue west, cross the intersection of {{ill|National Route 319|ja|国道319号|12=draft}} and {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 206|ja|県道206号|12=draft}} at Naeda, and proceed further west. After passing under the Dosan Line overpass, continue south along the Dosan Line. Then, without entering any alley between the {{ill|Takamatsu-Kotohira Electric Railway|ja|高松琴平電気鉄道|12=draft}} ({{ill|Kotoden|ja|高松琴平電気鉄道琴平線|lt=Kotohira Line|lt_ja=琴平線|12=draft}}) and the Dosan Line, cross the Yokose level crossing; if you continue straight south, you will reach the '''High Lantern''' situated in the park “Kita Shin'en” on the east side of {{ill|Kotoden Kotohira Station|ja|琴電琴平駅|12=draft}}, marking the end of the main highway.<ref>Refer to the brochure “Konpira Kaidō” (published by the Konpira Pilgrimage Guide Council).</ref> From the High Lantern, if you cross {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 207|ja|県道207号|12=draft}} and proceed straight south along Kotohira’s urban lanes, then at the intersection with the shopping arcade turn west (a right turn) and continue, you will enter the approach to Konpira Shrine.

<gallery>
File:Noboru Segawa-KonpiraKouTourou.jpg|Taisuke lantern at {{ill|Marugame Port|ja|丸亀港|12=draft}}
File:Marugame kaidou.jpg|Torii (Nakabu, Marugame City)
</gallery>

=== Konpira Orai ===
[[File:Konpira orai sign.jpg|thumb|200px|Sign of Konpira Orai (Hayashima Town)]]
{|
|-
|{{Ja_Route_Sign|30}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=165}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=21}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=22}}
|}
In the central area of Bizen Province, around the {{ill|Okayama Domain|ja|岡山藩|12=draft}} (near present-day {{ill|Okayama Prefecture|ja|岡山県|12=draft}}, {{ill|Okayama City|ja|岡山市|12=draft}}, {{ill|Kita Ward|ja|北区 (岡山市)|lt=Kita Ward|lt_ja=北区|12=draft}}, and the {{ill|Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|ja|岡山表町商店街|12=draft}}), or from Itakuramura Mashin of the {{ill|Niwase Domain|ja|庭瀬藩|12=draft}}, located near {{ill|Kibitsu Station|ja|吉備津駅|12=draft}} (the junction of the former {{ill|Sanyōdō|ja|山陽道|12=draft}}), a route extends via {{ill|Hayashima Town|ja|早島町|lt=Hayashima|12=draft}}, {{ill|Chayamachi District|ja|茶屋町地区|lt=Chayamachi|12=draft}}, {{ill|Fujito District|ja|藤戸地区|lt=Fujito|12=draft}}, {{ill|Yukayama|ja|由加山|12=draft}}, {{ill|Kojima Area (Kurashiki)|ja|児島地域 (倉敷市)|lt=Kojima|12=draft}}, and {{ill|Shimotsui District|ja|下津井地区|lt=Shimotsui|12=draft}}, and by ferry ({{ill|Ferry|ja|渡し船|12=draft}}) joins the above-mentioned Marugame Kaidō. In particular, with respect to the route originating from the Okayama Domain, it is counted among the six known as the '''Okayama Domain Six Official Routes'''<ref>“Konpira Orai” (prototype of {{ill|National Route 30|ja|国道30号|12=draft}}, the '''main route'''); “Kamogata Orai” (prototype of {{ill|National Route 2|ja|国道2号|12=draft}}); “Matsuyama Orai” (prototype of {{ill|National Route 180|ja|国道180号|12=draft}}—overlapping with {{ill|Sanyōdō|ja|山陽道|12=draft}} along the way); “Kurashiki Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 27 Okayama-Yoshii Line|ja|岡山県道27号岡山吉井線|12=draft}}); “Tsuyama Orai” (prototype of {{ill|National Route 53|ja|国道53号|12=draft}}); and “Ushimado Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 28|ja|岡山県道28号|12=draft}}).</ref> Furthermore, since this route—beyond Hayashima—passes through Yukayama, a local center of faith, it has preserved the custom of '''dual pilgrimage''', whereby pilgrims visit both {{ill|Main Yuka Shrine|ja|由加神社本宮|12=draft}} and {{ill|Rendai-ji|ja|蓮台寺 (倉敷市)|lt=Rendai-ji|lt_ja=蓮台寺|12=draft}} (associated with {{ill|Yuga Daigongen|ja|瑜伽大権現|12=draft}}) for protection against misfortune before proceeding to Konpira.

