=== Konpira Orai ===
[[File:Konpira orai sign.jpg|thumb|200px|Sign of Konpira Orai (Hayashima Town)]]
{|
|-
|{{Ja_Route_Sign|30}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=165}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=21}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=22}}
|}
In the central area of Bizen Province, around the {{ill|Okayama Domain|ja|岡山藩|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Domain|qq=}} (near present-day {{ill|Okayama Prefecture|ja|岡山県|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Prefecture|qq=}}, {{ill|Okayama City|ja|岡山市|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama City|qq=}}, {{ill|Kita Ward|ja|北区 (岡山市)|lt=Kita Ward|lt_ja=北区|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kita Ward|qq=}}, and the {{ill|Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|ja|岡山表町商店街|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|qq=}}), or from Itakuramura Mashin of the {{ill|Niwase Domain|ja|庭瀬藩|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Niwase Domain|qq=}}, located near {{ill|Kibitsu Station|ja|吉備津駅|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kibitsu Station|qq=}} (the junction of the former {{ill|Sanyōdō|ja|山陽道|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sanyōdō|qq=}}), a route extends via {{ill|Hayashima Town|ja|早島町|lt=Hayashima|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hayashima Town|qq=}}, {{ill|Chayamachi District|ja|茶屋町地区|lt=Chayamachi|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chayamachi District|qq=}}, {{ill|Fujito District|ja|藤戸地区|lt=Fujito|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fujito District|qq=}}, {{ill|Yukayama|ja|由加山|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yukayama|qq=}}, {{ill|Kojima Area (Kurashiki)|ja|児島地域 (倉敷市)|lt=Kojima|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kojima Area (Kurashiki)|qq=}}, and {{ill|Shimotsui District|ja|下津井地区|lt=Shimotsui|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shimotsui District|qq=}}, and by ferry ({{ill|Ferry|ja|渡し船|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ferry|qq=}}) joins the above-mentioned Marugame Kaidō. In particular, with respect to the route originating from the Okayama Domain, it is counted among the six known as the '''Okayama Domain Six Official Routes'''<ref>“Konpira Orai” (prototype of {{ill|National Route 30|ja|国道30号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/National Route 30|qq=}}, the '''main route'''); “Kamogata Orai” (prototype of {{ill|National Route 2|ja|国道2号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/National Route 2|qq=}}); “Matsuyama Orai” (prototype of {{ill|National Route 180|ja|国道180号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/National Route 180|qq=}}—overlapping with {{ill|Sanyōdō|ja|山陽道|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sanyōdō|qq=}} along the way); “Kurashiki Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 27 Okayama-Yoshii Line|ja|岡山県道27号岡山吉井線|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Prefectural Route 27 Okayama-Yoshii Line|qq=}}); “Tsuyama Orai” (prototype of {{ill|National Route 53|ja|国道53号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/National Route 53|qq=}}); and “Ushimado Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 28|ja|岡山県道28号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Prefectural Route 28|qq=}}).</ref> Furthermore, since this route—beyond Hayashima—passes through Yukayama, a local center of faith, it has preserved the custom of '''dual pilgrimage''', whereby pilgrims visit both {{ill|Main Yuka Shrine|ja|由加神社本宮|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Main Yuka Shrine|qq=}} and {{ill|Rendai-ji|ja|蓮台寺 (倉敷市)|lt=Rendai-ji|lt_ja=蓮台寺|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Rendai-ji|qq=}} (associated with {{ill|Yuga Daigongen|ja|瑜伽大権現|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yuga Daigongen|qq=}}) for protection against misfortune before proceeding to Konpira.

