[[File:Kagawa_Pref_R282_祓川橋西.jpg|thumb|Torii on Takamatsu Kaidō (Mannou Town's {{ill|Kagawa Prefecture Route 282 Takamatsu-Kotohira Line|ja|香川県道282号高松琴平線|lt=Kagawa Prefecture Route 282|lt_ja=香川県道282号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefecture Route 282 Takamatsu-Kotohira Line|qq=}})]]
'''Konpira Kaidō''' (金毘羅街道) refers to the pilgrimage route developed to connect various regions with {{ill|Konpira Shrine|ja|金刀比羅宮|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Konpira Shrine|qq=}} (located in {{ill|Kagawa Prefecture|ja|香川県|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefecture|qq=}}, {{ill|Nakatado District|ja|仲多度郡|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nakatado District|qq=}}, {{ill|Kotohira Town|ja|琴平町|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kotohira Town|qq=}}) and is classified as a {{ill|Kaidō|ja|街道|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kaidō|qq=}}. Multiple routes exist, and in some regions it is also known as '''Konpira Ōrai''' (金毘羅往来).

Among them, the Takamatsu Kaidō, Marugame Kaidō, Tadotsu Kaidō, Awa Kaidō, and Iyo/Tosa Kaidō—which were particularly well used—are collectively known as the '''Konpira Five Highways''' (金毘羅五街道). In addition to these major routes, other roads used for pilgrimages to Konpira were also referred to as either Konpira Kaidō or Konpira Ōrai. In the following sections of this article, the pilgrimage routes and highways that are historically closely associated with the "Konpira Five Highways" and the related network will be explained.
==Overview==



{{ill|Konpira Kaido|ja|金毘羅街道|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Konpira Kaido|qq=}} is a pilgrimage route of {{ill|Kotohira Shrines|lt=Kotohira Shrines|ja|金刀比羅神社|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kotohira Shrines|qq=}} located in {{ill|Japan|simple|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Japan|qq=}}. It connects many Konpira Shrines<ref>{{Cite web|title=Arched Stone Bridge {{!|qq=draft}} FACILITIES {{!}} GUIDE |url=http://www.shikokumura.or.jp/en/guide/facilities/arched-stone-bridge/ |access-date=2023-09-17 |website=SHIKOKUMURA |language=ja}}</ref> on [[Shikoku]]<ref>https://www.skr.mlit.go.jp/kikaku/88-kei/en/scenery/50_ehime.html</ref>. It is a [[Kaidō]].

{{ill|Kotohira Shrines|ja|金刀比羅神社|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kotohira Shrines|qq=}} are [[shinto shrine]]s dedicated to [[Ōmononushi]]. Due to [[Shinbutsu-shūgō]] they often also worship [[Konpira Gongen]]

They are part of the famous Inahachikonten Shrines (稲八金天神社)  of the [[Shrine Consolidation Policy]] alongside [[Inari Shrine]], [[Hachiman shrine|Hachiman Shrine]], {{ill|Kotohira Shrines|ja|金刀比羅神社|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kotohira Shrines|qq=}}, and [[Tenmangū|Tenmangu Shrine]].

