Starting at an ichirizuka that once existed near the present {{ill|Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|ja|岡山表町商店街|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|qq=}} (former Sen'ami Bridge), the route proceeds west through the Omotecho 3-chōme Shopping District, then heads south along {{ill|Yanagawa-suji|ja|柳川筋|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yanagawa-suji|qq=}}, turns west at the {{ill|Daionji Intersection|ja|大雲寺前停留場|lt=Daionji Intersection|lt_ja=大雲寺交差点|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Daionji Intersection|qq=}}, then continues southwest via the Daiku Intersection (in front of Okayama City Hall), passes to the west of the north side of {{ill|Ōmoto Station|ja|大元駅|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōmoto Station|qq=}}, and then heads south along the tracks of the {{ill|Uno Line|ja|宇野線|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Uno Line|qq=}} toward Hayashima.<ref name="k-ourai" /> It is a direct route from the center of Okayama to Yukayama and Konpira. From Hayashima (at the Matsuosaka Intersection) onward, it coincides with the route described below for the Niwase Konpira Orai.

