== '''Marugame Kaidō''' (丸亀街道) (Konpira Orai, 金毘羅往来)
==
{| 
|-
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Kagawa|number=4|align=left}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Kagawa|number=204|align=left}} 
|}
Starting from {{ill|Marugame Port|ja|丸亀港|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Marugame Port|qq=}}, this route proceeds via Nakabu, Gunke, Yokita, and others to Kotohira. Because the overland distance was short and the terrain flat, many pilgrims—arriving by {{ill|Konpira Ship|ja|金毘羅船|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Konpira Ship|qq=}} from places such as {{ill|Osaka|ja|大坂|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Osaka|qq=}} or from {{ill|Bizen Province|ja|備前国|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Bizen Province|qq=}}—used it. It is said that during the {{ill|Enkyō era|ja|延享|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Enkyō era|qq=}} a regular ship service operated between Osaka and Marugame, making it the busiest of the many Konpira Kaidō routes. Today, roads following its course include {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 204 Marugame Station Line|ja|香川県道204号丸亀停車場線|lt=Kagawa Prefectural Route 204|lt_ja=香川県道204号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefectural Route 204 Marugame Station Line|qq=}} and {{ill|Kagawa/Tokushima Prefectural Route 4 Marugame-Miyoshi Line|ja|香川県道・徳島県道4号丸亀三好線|lt=Prefectural Route 4|lt_ja=香川県道4号|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa/Tokushima Prefectural Route 4 Marugame-Miyoshi Line|qq=}}.

At {{ill|Marugame Port|ja|丸亀港|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Marugame Port|qq=}}, from the Taisuke lantern or from the {{ill|Sanuki Hamakaidō|ja|さぬき浜街道|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sanuki Hamakaidō|qq=}} ({{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 193 Kawazu-Marugame Line|ja|香川県道193号川津丸亀線|lt=Kagawa Prefectural Route 193|lt_ja=香川県道193号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefectural Route 193 Kawazu-Marugame Line|qq=}}) beneath the Kyogoku Ohashi—where {{ill|Kyogoku Funatama Shrine|ja|京極船魂神社|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kyogoku Funatama Shrine|qq=}} is located—head south along a municipal road toward {{ill|Marugame Station|ja|丸亀駅|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Marugame Station|qq=}}. Pass under the elevated structure of the {{ill|Yosan Line|ja|予讃線|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yosan Line|qq=}}, and at Tsūchō turn west. In front of Marugame Station, after crossing {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 204 Marugame Station Line|ja|香川県道204号丸亀停車場線|lt=Kagawa Prefectural Route 204|lt_ja=香川県道204号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefectural Route 204 Marugame Station Line|qq=}}, immediately enter the museum street of Hamamachi (a narrow lane located about 50 m west of the intersection—with the south side of the {{ill|Inokuma Genichirō Contemporary Art Museum|ja|猪熊弦一郎現代美術館|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Inokuma Genichirō Contemporary Art Museum|qq=}}) and proceed south through Nanjō Town to Nakabu Town. In Nakabu (at the marker of “Torinomeken”), turn west; however, the road descends to the southwest, passing through Nakabu’s large torii gate and continuing south. Then cross {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 205|ja|香川県道205号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefectural Route 205|qq=}}, and at the three‐way intersection of Nakabu’s three houses (marked by the Heisei-era five‐stone marker) turn east; next, cross {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 33|ja|香川県道33号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefectural Route 33|qq=}} and enter Yamakita Town. From the Castle West Community Center in Yamakita, turn south onto {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 204|ja|香川県道204号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefectural Route 204|qq=}} and enter Katsubaru Town; after passing in front of the Marugame Castle South Post Office, at a fork marked by the Heisei-era twenty-stone marker, turn west—leaving Prefectural Route 204 onto a municipal road along the town boundary—and proceed south. Cross {{ill|National Route 11|ja|国道11号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/National Route 11|qq=}}, pass along the eastern edge of Tamura Pond (a local reservoir, {{ill|Reservoir|ja|溜め池|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Reservoir|qq=}}), and continue further south; then, passing under the Takamatsu Expressway overpass where a lantern is visible on the west side of the road, proceed south toward Gunke Town. In Sanjō Town, merge with {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 4|ja|香川県道4号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefectural Route 4|qq=}} and enter Yokita Town in {{ill|Zentsūji City|ja|善通寺市|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Zentsūji City|qq=}}. Thereafter, continuing almost along Route 4, from Yokita Town pass through {{ill|Mannou Town|ja|まんのう町|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mannou Town|qq=}} (Kōmon and Mannou Town Nishitakashino) and at Naeda in {{ill|Kotohira Town|ja|琴平町|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kotohira Town|qq=}}, turn west. After passing through the precinct alley of {{ill|Wakamiya Shrine|ja|若宮神社|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Wakamiya Shrine|qq=}}, continue west, cross the intersection of {{ill|National Route 319|ja|国道319号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/National Route 319|qq=}} and {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 206|ja|県道206号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefectural Route 206|qq=}} at Naeda, and proceed further west. After passing under the Dosan Line overpass, continue south along the Dosan Line. Then, without entering any alley between the {{ill|Takamatsu-Kotohira Electric Railway|ja|高松琴平電気鉄道|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takamatsu-Kotohira Electric Railway|qq=}} ({{ill|Kotoden|ja|高松琴平電気鉄道琴平線|lt=Kotohira Line|lt_ja=琴平線|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kotoden|qq=}}) and the Dosan Line, cross the Yokose level crossing; if you continue straight south, you will reach the '''High Lantern''' situated in the park “Kita Shin'en” on the east side of {{ill|Kotoden Kotohira Station|ja|琴電琴平駅|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kotoden Kotohira Station|qq=}}, marking the end of the main highway.<ref>Refer to the brochure “Konpira Kaidō” (published by the Konpira Pilgrimage Guide Council).</ref> From the High Lantern, if you cross {{ill|Kagawa Prefectural Route 207|ja|県道207号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kagawa Prefectural Route 207|qq=}} and proceed straight south along Kotohira’s urban lanes, then at the intersection with the shopping arcade turn west (a right turn) and continue, you will enter the approach to Konpira Shrine.

