=== Konpira Orai ===
[[File:Konpira orai sign.jpg|thumb|200px|Sign of Konpira Orai (Hayashima Town)]]
{|
|-
|{{Ja_Route_Sign|30}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=165}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=21}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=22}}
|}
In the central area of Bizen Province, around the [[:en:Okayama Domain|Okayama Domain]] (near present-day [[:en:Okayama Prefecture|Okayama Prefecture]], [[:en:Okayama|Okayama City]], [[:en:Kita-ku, Okayama|Kita Ward]], and the {{ill|Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|ja|岡山表町商店街|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|qq=}}), or from Itakuramura Mashin of the [[:en:Niwase Domain|Niwase Domain]], located near [[:en:Kibitsu Station|Kibitsu Station]] (the junction of the former [[:en:San'yōdō|Sanyōdō]]), a route extends via [[:en:Hayashima|Hayashima]], {{ill|Chayamachi District|ja|茶屋町地区|lt=Chayamachi|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chayamachi District|qq=}}, {{ill|Fujito District|ja|藤戸地区|lt=Fujito|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fujito District|qq=}}, {{ill|Yukayama|ja|由加山|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yukayama|qq=}}, {{ill|Kojima Area (Kurashiki)|ja|児島地域 (倉敷市)|lt=Kojima|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kojima Area (Kurashiki)|qq=}}, and {{ill|Shimotsui District|ja|下津井地区|lt=Shimotsui|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shimotsui District|qq=}}, and by ferry ({{ill|Ferry|ja|渡し船|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ferry|qq=}}) joins the above-mentioned Marugame Kaidō. In particular, with respect to the route originating from the Okayama Domain, it is counted among the six known as the '''Okayama Domain Six Official Routes'''<ref>“Konpira Orai” (prototype of [[:en:Japan National Route 30|National Route 30]], the '''main route'''); “Kamogata Orai” (prototype of [[:en:Japan National Route 2|National Route 2]]); “Matsuyama Orai” (prototype of [[:en:Japan National Route 180|National Route 180]]—overlapping with [[:en:San'yōdō|Sanyōdō]] along the way); “Kurashiki Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 27 Okayama-Yoshii Line|ja|岡山県道27号岡山吉井線|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Prefectural Route 27 Okayama-Yoshii Line|qq=}}); “Tsuyama Orai” (prototype of [[:en:Japan National Route 53|National Route 53]]); and “Ushimado Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 28|ja|岡山県道28号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Prefectural Route 28|qq=}}).</ref> Furthermore, since this route—beyond Hayashima—passes through Yukayama, a local center of faith, it has preserved the custom of '''dual pilgrimage''', whereby pilgrims visit both {{ill|Main Yuka Shrine|ja|由加神社本宮|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Main Yuka Shrine|qq=}} and {{ill|Rendai-ji|ja|蓮台寺 (倉敷市)|lt=Rendai-ji|lt_ja=蓮台寺|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Rendai-ji|qq=}} (associated with {{ill|Yuga Daigongen|ja|瑜伽大権現|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yuga Daigongen|qq=}}) for protection against misfortune before proceeding to Konpira.

