From the “Nudagawa Road Marker,” where the Niwase and Kibitsu Konpira Orais converge, the route heads west through residential areas, crosses the {{ill|Ashimori River|ja|足守川|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ashimori River|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 笹ヶ瀬川}}, and continues south along a municipal road near Okayama Prefectural Route 153 before merging with it. It then descends southwest along the north side of the hill on which the Okayama Prefectural General Distribution Center stands, crosses [[:en:Japan National Route 2|National Route 2]] and the {{ill|Okayama Bypass|ja|岡山バイパス|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Bypass|qq=}} in the Muzu area, and via Okayama Prefectural Route 185 reaches [[:en:Hayashima|Hayashima]]. At Matsuosaka Intersection it merges with the Meo Konpira Orai and joins Okayama Prefectural Route 152; at the intersection with Route 165 it turns south toward {{ill|Chayamachi District|ja|茶屋町地区|lt=Chayamachi|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chayamachi District|qq=}} and {{ill|Fujito District|ja|藤戸地区|lt=Fujito|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fujito District|qq=}}. From Fujito, the route continues further south, detouring broadly along the coast of the Seto Inland Sea at the foot of [[:en:Mount Washu|Washiyama]], and (in some cases, after passing a tunnel known as the '''Ouginone Tunnels''' located on the mid-slope of Washiyama beyond the Kojima urban area) descends the mountain to the port. From {{ill|Shimotsui Port|ja|下津井港|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shimotsui Port|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 下津井地区}}, a ferry takes travelers onto the Marugame Kaidō.

