=== Konpira Orai ===
[[File:Konpira orai sign.jpg|thumb|200px|Sign of Konpira Orai (Hayashima Town)]]
{|
|-
|{{Ja_Route_Sign|30}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=165}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=21}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=22}}
|}
In the central area of Bizen Province, around the [[:en:Okayama Domain|Okayama Domain]] (near present-day [[:en:Okayama Prefecture|Okayama Prefecture]], [[:en:Okayama|Okayama City]], [[:en:Kita-ku, Okayama|Kita Ward]], and the {{ill|Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|ja|岡山表町商店街|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|qq=|1=Omotechō Shōtengai|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11472751}}), or from Itakuramura Mashin of the [[:en:Niwase Domain|Niwase Domain]], located near [[:en:Kibitsu Station|Kibitsu Station]] (the junction of the former [[:en:San'yōdō|Sanyōdō]]), a route extends via [[:en:Hayashima|Hayashima]], {{ill|Chayamachi District|ja|茶屋町地区|lt=Chayamachi|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chayamachi District|qq=|1=Chayamachi Area|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11617964}}, {{ill|Fujito District|ja|藤戸地区|lt=Fujito|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fujito District|qq=|1=Fujito|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11624064}}, {{ill|Yukayama|ja|由加山|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yukayama|qq=|1=Yuga Mountain|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11577570}}, {{ill|Kojima Area (Kurashiki)|ja|児島地域 (倉敷市)|lt=Kojima|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kojima Area (Kurashiki)|qq=|1=Kojima Area|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11388647}}, and {{ill|Shimotsui District|ja|下津井地区|lt=Shimotsui|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shimotsui District|qq=|1=Shimotsui|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11361095}}, and by ferry ({{ill|Ferry|ja|渡し船|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ferry|qq=|1=flat-bottomed ferry|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q2878108}}) joins the above-mentioned Marugame Kaidō. In particular, with respect to the route originating from the Okayama Domain, it is counted among the six known as the '''Okayama Domain Six Official Routes'''<ref>“Konpira Orai” (prototype of [[:en:Japan National Route 30|National Route 30]], the '''main route'''); “Kamogata Orai” (prototype of [[:en:Japan National Route 2|National Route 2]]); “Matsuyama Orai” (prototype of [[:en:Japan National Route 180|National Route 180]]—overlapping with [[:en:San'yōdō|Sanyōdō]] along the way); “Kurashiki Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 27 Okayama-Yoshii Line|ja|岡山県道27号岡山吉井線|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Prefectural Route 27 Okayama-Yoshii Line|qq=|1=Okayama Prefectural Road Route 27|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11472480}}); “Tsuyama Orai” (prototype of [[:en:Japan National Route 53|National Route 53]]); and “Ushimado Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 28|ja|岡山県道28号|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Prefectural Route 28|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 岡山県道28号岡山牛窓線|1=Okayama Prefectural Road Route 28|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11472488}}).</ref> Furthermore, since this route—beyond Hayashima—passes through Yukayama, a local center of faith, it has preserved the custom of '''dual pilgrimage''', whereby pilgrims visit both {{ill|Main Yuka Shrine|ja|由加神社本宮|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Main Yuka Shrine|qq=|1=Yuga-jinja|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11577571}} and {{ill|Rendai-ji|ja|蓮台寺 (倉敷市)|lt=Rendai-ji|lt_ja=蓮台寺|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Rendai-ji|qq=|1=Rendai-Ji (Kurashiki)|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11621649}} (associated with {{ill|Yuga Daigongen|ja|瑜伽大権現|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yuga Daigongen|qq=}}) for protection against misfortune before proceeding to Konpira.

