=== Konpira Orai ===
[[File:Konpira orai sign.jpg|thumb|200px|Sign of Konpira Orai (Hayashima Town)]]
{|
|-
|{{Ja_Route_Sign|30}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=165}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=21}}
|{{Ja_Pref_Route_Sign|pref=Okayama|number=22}}
|}
In the central area of Bizen Province, around the {{ill|Okayama Domain|en|Okayama Domain|qid=Q903497|lt=Okayama Domain|1=Okayama Domain}} (near present-day {{ill|Okayama Prefecture|en|Okayama Prefecture|qid=Q132936|lt=Okayama Prefecture|1=Okayama Prefecture}}, {{ill|Okayama|en|Okayama|qid=Q200078|lt=Okayama City|1=Okayama}}, {{ill|Kita-ku, Okayama|en|Kita-ku, Okayama|qid=Q855478|lt=Kita Ward|1=Kita-ku, Okayama}}, and the {{ill|Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|ja|岡山表町商店街|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Omotecho Shopping Street|1=Omotechō Shōtengai|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11472751}}), or from Itakuramura Mashin of the {{ill|Niwase Domain|en|Niwase Domain|qid=Q3034514|lt=Niwase Domain|1=Niwase Domain}}, located near {{ill|Kibitsu Station|en|Kibitsu Station|qid=Q6404041|lt=Kibitsu Station|1=Kibitsu Station}} (the junction of the former {{ill|San'yōdō|en|San'yōdō|qid=Q1376722|lt=Sanyōdō|1=San'yōdō}}), a route extends via {{ill|Hayashima|en|Hayashima|qid=Q1155361|lt=Hayashima|1=Hayashima}}, {{ill|Chayamachi District|ja|茶屋町地区|lt=Chayamachi|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chayamachi District|1=Chayamachi Area|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11617964}}, {{ill|Fujito District|ja|藤戸地区|lt=Fujito|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fujito District|1=Fujito|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11624064}}, {{ill|Yukayama|ja|由加山|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yukayama|1=Yuga Mountain|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11577570}}, {{ill|Kojima Area (Kurashiki)|ja|児島地域 (倉敷市)|lt=Kojima|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kojima Area (Kurashiki)|1=Kojima Area|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11388647}}, and {{ill|Shimotsui District|ja|下津井地区|lt=Shimotsui|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shimotsui District|1=Shimotsui|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11361095}}, and by ferry ({{ill|Ferry|ja|渡し船|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ferry|1=flat-bottomed ferry|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q2878108}}) joins the above-mentioned Marugame Kaidō. In particular, with respect to the route originating from the Okayama Domain, it is counted among the six known as the '''Okayama Domain Six Official Routes'''<ref>“Konpira Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Japan National Route 30|en|Japan National Route 30|qid=Q11421442|lt=National Route 30|1=Japan National Route 30}}, the '''main route'''); “Kamogata Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Japan National Route 2|en|Japan National Route 2|qid=Q1131340|lt=National Route 2|1=Japan National Route 2}}); “Matsuyama Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Japan National Route 180|en|Japan National Route 180|qid=Q6156873|lt=National Route 180|1=Japan National Route 180}}—overlapping with {{ill|San'yōdō|en|San'yōdō|qid=Q1376722|lt=Sanyōdō|1=San'yōdō}} along the way); “Kurashiki Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 27 Okayama-Yoshii Line|ja|岡山県道27号岡山吉井線|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Prefectural Route 27 Okayama-Yoshii Line|1=Okayama Prefectural Road Route 27|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11472480}}); “Tsuyama Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Japan National Route 53|en|Japan National Route 53|qid=Q6157735|lt=National Route 53|1=Japan National Route 53}}); and “Ushimado Orai” (prototype of {{ill|Okayama Prefectural Route 28|ja|岡山県道28号|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Okayama Prefectural Route 28|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 岡山県道28号岡山牛窓線|1=Okayama Prefectural Road Route 28|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11472488}}).</ref> Furthermore, since this route—beyond Hayashima—passes through Yukayama, a local center of faith, it has preserved the custom of '''dual pilgrimage''', whereby pilgrims visit both {{ill|Main Yuka Shrine|ja|由加神社本宮|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Main Yuka Shrine|1=Yuga Shrine|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11577571}} and {{ill|Rendai-ji|ja|蓮台寺 (倉敷市)|lt=Rendai-ji|lt_ja=蓮台寺|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Rendai-ji|1=Yugasan Rendaiji|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11621649}} (associated with {{ill|Yuga Daigongen|ja|瑜伽大権現|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yuga Daigongen|qq=}}) for protection against misfortune before proceeding to Konpira.

